      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p><strong>SPECIMEN :</strong>&nbsp; Paraffin block</p>\n<p><strong>IHC NO : 436/2024</strong></p>\n<p><strong>RESULT :&nbsp; </strong>Requested marker : <strong>EBV (EBER) BY CISH - Negative</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Clinical Notes :&nbsp;</strong>Pain in abdomen. Large cell lymphoma (generalised lymphadenopathy). Patient is HIV Positive.</p>\n<p><strong>Gross Examination :&nbsp;</strong>Received one paraffin block and one stained slide labelled as 24.2662.</p>\n<p><br><strong>Processing Method</strong>: Manual staining</p>\n<p><strong>Staining:</strong> EBER</p>\n<p><strong>Result interpretation :</strong><br>&bull; EBER by CISH is performed on formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded tissues and the result is very similar to the&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;traditional IHC slide - a brown (DAB) chromogen target location on a Haematoxylin counter-stained slide.<br>&bull; The technique demonstrates cells latently-infected with EBV as it hybridizes to abundantly express Epstein-Barr virus-encoded RNA (EBER) transcripts which are concentrated in the nuclei of latently-infected cells.</p>\n<p><strong>Quality Assurance :</strong><br>&bull; The external control has been found to be satisfactory.<br>&bull; CISH has been performed using the Zytofast EBV probe(PF29) for detection of EBER.</p>\n<p><strong>Dispatch Summary :</strong><br>1. Blocks that are submitted are enclosed with the report.<br>2. Stained slide is archived.<br>3. Case images are available on request.</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
      "_id": "679a0a8b52a2bef040e80f60"
    }
